WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.571
Least privilege starts with
choosing how the agent acts:

2
00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:07.767
for a user when someone's present, as
itself only when there's a reason,

3
00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:11.663
and with its own user account only
when it truly needs a mailbox.

4
00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:16.128
Microsoft blocks the most dangerous
roles and permissions for agents,

5
00:00:16.128 --> 00:00:18.474
but that's a floor, not least privilege.

6
00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:21.988
Agents can still hold roles that
are privileged in your tenant,

7
00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.150
so apply your own risk classification.

8
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.744
Keep inherited permissions
narrow, because one broad

9
00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:31.738
setting turns every future grant
into a grant to every agent.

10
00:00:31.738 --> 00:00:34.426
And no agent holds a
standing privileged role.

11
00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:38.162
If it seems to need one permanently,
that's a design defect.

12
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:39.480
Next, policy.
